WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.603
"The judging starts in an hour and a half?" Nathan cried.

2
00:00:17.604 --> 00:00:21.757
"Oh no! What if we don't find my painting in time?"

3
00:00:21.758 --> 00:00:26.695
"Don't worry. The Lemonade Detectives are on the case," Maggie assured him.

4
00:00:26.696 --> 00:00:29.186
"Come on, guys. Let's get started!"

5
00:00:29.187 --> 00:00:34.165
Henry nodded. "First we should look for Patrick near his painting.

6
00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:37.129
Then we can look for Mr. Collins."

7
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:41.569
"Hannah is probably still at her family's booth," Cole added.

8
00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:45.890
"And what about that weird woman? We don't know where to find her."

9
00:00:45.891 --> 00:00:50.107
"Maybe she'll go back to the stand for her lemonade," Maggie said.

10
00:00:50.108 --> 00:00:52.855
"She already paid for it, remember?"

11
00:00:52.856 --> 00:00:58.579
Henry nodded. "Why don't you go back to the lemonade stand?" he told Maggie.

12
00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:02.713
"You can keep selling lemonade while you watch for all our suspects."

13
00:01:02.714 --> 00:01:06.794
"Especially the sunglasses woman," Cole said.

14
00:01:06.795 --> 00:01:11.705
"Good idea." Maggie hurried off.

15
00:01:11.706 --> 00:01:15.972
"I know where Patrick's painting is hanging," Nathan told Henry and Cole.

16
00:01:15.973 --> 00:01:20.808
"Come on, I'll show you."

17
00:01:20.809 --> 00:01:24.510
Nathan led the way to another section of the art show.

18
00:01:24.511 --> 00:01:28.865
Patrick's painting was an oil painting of a pretty pond at sunset.

19
00:01:28.866 --> 00:01:33.327
"Wow, he really is good," Cole said, studying the painting.

20
00:01:33.328 --> 00:01:36.544
"Do you think this painting will end up in the museum?"

21
00:01:36.545 --> 00:01:38.845
"Never mind that," Henry said.

22
00:01:38.846 --> 00:01:46.667
"I don't see Patrick around here. Let's look for Hannah."

23
00:01:46.668 --> 00:01:50.646
At the crafts show, Hannah was still at the basket-weaving booth.

24
00:01:50.647 --> 00:01:53.412
She smiled when she saw the boys coming.

25
00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:57.333
"Hi, lemonade gang," she said. "Where's Maggie?"

26
00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.613
"Selling lemonade," Henry said.

27
00:01:59.614 --> 00:02:03.037
"What have you been doing since we saw you last?"

28
00:02:03.038 --> 00:02:07.779
Hannah looked confused. "The same thing I've been doing all day."

29
00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:10.477
She held up the basket she was weaving.

30
00:02:10.478 --> 00:02:15.241
"Making baskets, selling baskets, and talking about baskets."

31
00:02:15.242 --> 00:02:19.289
"Did you leave this booth to go anywhere?" Cole asked.

32
00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:23.936
"Like over to the art show, for instance?" Nathan added hopefully.

33
00:02:23.937 --> 00:02:27.571
"I went to the bathroom once." Hannah frowned.

34
00:02:27.572 --> 00:02:32.453
"Why are you guys so interested in what I've been doing?" Suddenly she gasped.

35
00:02:32.454 --> 00:02:38.200
"Wait! Are you investigating a mystery? Am I a suspect?"

36
00:02:38.201 --> 00:02:44.921
Henry sighed. That was the only problem with The Lemonade Detectives' success in solving mysteries.

37
00:02:44.922 --> 00:02:47.803
Everyone in town had heard about them by now.

38
00:02:47.804 --> 00:02:50.455
It made it hard to interview people.

39
00:02:50.456 --> 00:02:55.163
"Actually, we are investigating a mystery," he admitted.

40
00:02:55.164 --> 00:02:57.752
"Nathan's painting disappeared."

41
00:02:57.753 --> 00:03:04.110
"Oh." Hannah stared at Nathan with a slight frown. "You entered the art show?"

42
00:03:04.111 --> 00:03:06.485
"Yes," Nathan said.

43
00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:10.348
"And we heard the judges love his painting," Cole added.

44
00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:15.815
"He might end up winning a spot in the museum. It's a huge honor, you know!"

45
00:03:15.816 --> 00:03:18.087
Hannah was still frowning.

46
00:03:18.088 --> 00:03:24.584
"Excuse me," she said, tossing her half-woven basket aside. "I have to go."

47
00:03:24.585 --> 00:03:27.044
"Wait!" Henry exclaimed.

48
00:03:27.046 --> 00:03:28.594
But it was too late.

49
00:03:28.595 --> 00:03:32.562
Hannah rushed off and disappeared around the corner of the next booth.

50
00:03:32.563 --> 00:03:36.290
"That was weird," Cole said, staring after her.

51
00:03:36.291 --> 00:03:39.799
"Do you think she ran off because she feels guilty?"

52
00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.388
"Maybe," Henry said.

53
00:03:42.389 --> 00:03:47.831
"Or maybe she was insulted that we were accusing her of stealing Nathan's painting."

54
00:03:47.832 --> 00:03:51.902
Nathan bit his lip. "What do we do now?

55
00:03:51.903 --> 00:03:55.344
The judging starts in an hour and ten minutes."

56
00:03:55.345 --> 00:03:59.225
"Let's look for our other suspects," Henry said.

57
00:03:59.226 --> 00:04:06.677
"We can question Hannah again later if necessary."

58
00:04:06.678 --> 00:04:09.135
They hurried back to the art show.

59
00:04:09.136 --> 00:04:13.109
But there was still no sign of Patrick or Mr. Collins.

60
00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:17.574
The park was more crowded than ever as people arrived for the art judging.

61
00:04:17.575 --> 00:04:23.563
Every year people in town loved to join the march over to the museum to display the winning artwork.

62
00:04:23.564 --> 00:04:26.355
"Now what?" Cole said.

63
00:04:26.356 --> 00:04:28.039
Henry looked at Nathan.

64
00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:32.212
"Why don't you go see if anyone returned your painting?" he said.

65
00:04:32.213 --> 00:04:34.918
"Cole and I will check in with Maggie."

66
00:04:34.919 --> 00:04:40.945
"Okay." Nathan didn't look very hopeful as he hurried off.

67
00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:46.473
Maggie was pouring lemonade for a middle-aged couple when Henry and Cole arrived.

68
00:04:46.474 --> 00:04:50.244
"Any news?" she asked as soon as the couple left.

69
00:04:50.245 --> 00:04:55.721
Henry shook his head. "We still haven't found Patrick or Mr. Collins.

70
00:04:55.722 --> 00:05:00.022
We did find Hannah, but we only talked to her for a minute."

71
00:05:00.023 --> 00:05:03.201
He quickly described the encounter with Hannah.

72
00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:07.084
"Have you seen any of our suspects?" Cole asked Maggie.

73
00:05:07.085 --> 00:05:12.437
"Nope." Maggie patted the cashbox. "I've sold a lot of lemonade.

74
00:05:12.438 --> 00:05:15.968
But I haven't seen anything suspicious at all."

75
00:05:15.969 --> 00:05:20.854
"The woman with the sunglasses didn't come back for her lemonade?" Henry asked.

76
00:05:20.855 --> 00:05:23.170
"Nope," Maggie said again.

77
00:05:23.171 --> 00:05:26.847
Just then Nora hurried over to the lemonade stand.

78
00:05:26.848 --> 00:05:30.297
"It's not right!" she announced loudly.

79
00:05:30.298 --> 00:05:33.018
"About the painting of Patches, I mean."

80
00:05:33.019 --> 00:05:36.773
Henry was too distracted to pay much attention to Nora.

81
00:05:36.774 --> 00:05:42.688
"We know," he told her. "We're trying to find Nathan's painting. Don't worry."

82
00:05:42.689 --> 00:05:46.596
"No!" Nora's voice was louder than ever.

83
00:05:46.597 --> 00:05:53.283
"It's not right! Patches is my kitty. She shouldn't be in a museum.

84
00:05:53.284 --> 00:05:58.799
She's mine—all mine! And the picture of her is mine too!"

85
00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:04.158
Spinning around, Nora raced away.
